.TH CS 1 "2026-10-29" "cs 1.12.3" "Claude Session Manager"
.SH NAME
cs \- manage Claude Code sessions across multiple hosts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cs
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cs
aggregates Claude Code session metadata from multiple Linux hosts into a
central MongoDB database, enabling cross-machine session visibility, tagging,
persistent tmux-backed sessions, and remote attach.
.PP
Sessions launched via
.B cs launch
run inside detached tmux sessions that survive SSH disconnects. Session state
(WORKING, WAITING, IDLE, DEAD) is detected from tmux pane content. Any session
can be reconnected from any machine via
.BR "cs attach" ,
which automatically SSH's to the remote host when necessary.
.PP
Running
.B cs
with no arguments displays a smart dashboard showing active sessions, recent
activity, and sessions needing attention.
.SH COMMANDS
.\" BEGIN GENERATED COMMANDS — edit commands.ts, run: bun scripts/gen-docs.ts
.TP
.BI "cs" " [\-\-sort [field]] [\-\-orphans]"
Display the local dashboard: a single merged table of this machine's sessions
with live tmux state overlaid on database records. No duplicates. Falls back
to a tmux\-only display if MongoDB is unreachable.
.RS
.PP
With \fB\-\-orphans\fP, also lists untracked tmux sessions that are running
Claude but have no database record (e.g. sessions started manually outside
cs).
.PP
\fB\-\-sort [field]\fP orders the table as in \fBcs list\fP. The other \fBcs
list\fP options do not apply to the dashboard.
.RE
.TP
.BI "cs sync" " [\-\-quiet]"
Harvest session metadata from \fB~/.claude/projects/\fP and upsert it to
MongoDB. Detects active tmux sessions and their state.
.RS
.PP
With \fB\-\-quiet\fP, suppresses all output \(em this is the form the periodic
cron/LaunchAgent sync runs.
.RE
.TP
.BI "cs list" " [\-\-local] [\-\-host <name>] [\-\-project <name>] [\-\-limit <n>] [\-\-sort [field]]"
List sessions from the database, most recently updated first. Defaults to all
hosts.
.RS
.TP
.BI \-\-sort " [field]"
Sort by \fBtitle\fP, \fBupdated\fP, \fBhost\fP, or \fBproject\fP
(\fB\-\-sort\fP alone sorts by title). Ties are broken by the remaining fields
in that order.
.TP
.B \-\-local
Show sessions from this host only.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " <name>"
Filter to a specific host. Accepts short names (e.g. \fBdev\fP matches
\fBdev.example.com\fP).
.TP
.BI \-\-project " <name>"
Filter by project name.
.TP
.BI \-\-limit " <n>"
Maximum number of results (default: 40).
.RE
.TP
.BI "cs launch" " <project> [prompt]"
Start Claude Code in a detached tmux session. The session survives SSH
disconnects \(em Claude keeps working even if you close your terminal. If
\fBprompt\fP is given, it is passed to Claude as the initial message.
.RS
.PP
The output tells you the session name and how to reconnect.
.RE
.TP
.BI "cs adopt" " <id\-or\-name> [\-\-attach]"
Wrap an existing Claude session in a managed tmux session \(em use this to
take a session you started normally and make it persistent. The session is
resumed via \fBclaude \-\-resume\fP inside a detached tmux. With
\fB\-\-attach\fP, connects immediately after adopting.
.TP
.BI "cs attach" " <id\-or\-name> [\-\-host <name>] [\-\-latest]"
Reconnect to a session. If it is on the local machine, attaches to its tmux
session directly; if you are already inside tmux, uses \fBswitch\-client\fP to
avoid nesting. If it is on a remote machine, cs \fBssh\fP(1)'s there, creates
the tmux session if needed, and attaches. Requires SSH key authentication for
remote sessions.
.RS
.PP
Sessions can be identified by ID prefix (like \fBgit\fP(1)), \fB/rename\fP
name (exact match), or project name. When ambiguous, cs prefers the local
host's session; use \fB\-\-host\fP to disambiguate explicitly.
.PP
If the matches are still ambiguous but all belong to the same project, cs
lists them newest first and asks which to attach; pressing Enter picks the
most recently active. \fB\-\-latest\fP skips the question and attaches to the
most recently active one (required when stdin is not a terminal). Matches
spanning several projects are always an error.
.RE
.TP
.BI "cs kill" " <id\-or\-name> [\-\-host <name>]"
Terminate a tmux session, local or remote via SSH. Updates the session state
in MongoDB immediately. With \fB\-\-all\fP, kills every active session,
optionally filtered to one host.
.TP
.BI "cs kill \-\-all" " [\-\-host <name>]"
Kill all active sessions. Optionally filter to a specific host.
.TP
.B cs resume
Interactive session picker using \fBfzf\fP(1). Displays recent sessions from
the current machine and launches \fBclaude \-\-resume\fP for the one you
select.
.TP
.B cs last
Resume the most recent session on this machine \(em no picker, straight to
Claude. Equivalent to selecting the first item in \fBcs resume\fP.
.TP
.B cs status
Display the live state of every active cs tmux session on this machine. Reads
tmux directly; does not require MongoDB.
.RS
.TP
.B WORKING
(green) Claude is actively generating output.
.TP
.B WAITING
(yellow) Claude is waiting for user input or permission.
.TP
.B IDLE
(dim) Session is alive but has no recent activity.
.TP
.B DEAD
(red) tmux session no longer exists.
.RE
.TP
.BI "cs tag" " <id\-or\-name> <label>"
Apply a text label to a session for easy identification. Tags are stored in
MongoDB and shown in \fBcs list\fP output.
.TP
.BI "cs info" " <id\-or\-name>"
Display the full record for a single session: session ID, machine, project
path, title, \fB/rename\fP name (if any), tag, state, message count,
timestamps, tmux session name, summary, and schema version.
.TP
.B cs hosts
List every host that has synced sessions, with session counts and when each
was last seen.
.TP
.BI "cs rm" " <id\-or\-name>"
Soft\-delete a session: the record is marked with a \fBdeleted_at\fP
timestamp, so it no longer appears in listings, queries, or sync \(em and
\fBcs sync\fP will not bring it back. Local files are untouched. \fBcs rm
\-\-undo\fP restores it.
.TP
.BI "cs rm \-\-undo" " <id\-or\-name>"
Restore a soft\-deleted session.
.TP
.BI "cs prune" " [\-\-days N] [\-\-all]"
Bulk soft\-delete sessions that have no \fB/rename\fP name and no tag. Default
threshold is 30 days; \fB\-\-all\fP prunes regardless of age. \fBNamed,
tagged, and running sessions are never pruned.\fP
.TP
.BI "cs deleted" " [\-\-local] [\-\-host <name>]"
List soft\-deleted sessions with their deletion timestamps. Defaults to all
hosts. Restore any of them with \fBcs rm \-\-undo <id>\fP.
.TP
.BI "cs gc" " [\-\-yes]"
Collapse duplicate sessions. Sessions are grouped by project and host; the
most recently updated one in each group is kept and the older ones become GC
candidates. \fBAn older session that is still running in tmux is never
removed\fP \(em it is listed as kept instead. Without \fB\-\-yes\fP, shows
what would be removed.
.RS
.PP
This is a soft\-delete \(em no local files are touched, and anything removed
can be restored with \fBcs rm \-\-undo <id>\fP.
.RE
.TP
.BI "cs purge" " <pattern>... [\-\-yes] [\-\-all] [\-\-host <name>] [\-\-deleted]"
Hard delete sessions \(em removes MongoDB records, JSONL files, and session
directories. \fBIrreversible.\fP Without \fB\-\-yes\fP, shows what would be
deleted. Must be run on the host where the sessions live.
.RS
.PP
Several sessions can be named at once (\fBcs purge \-\-yes s1 s2 s3\fP). Each
is resolved independently; one that does not resolve is reported and skipped
rather than aborting the batch.
.PP
With \fB\-\-all\fP, bulk deletes matching sessions (requires typed \fBYES\fP
confirmation). Bulk mode \fBskips live \fB/rename\fPd or tagged sessions\fP
unless they have already been soft\-deleted \(em a wildcard cannot silently
destroy a session you named or tagged. To purge one anyway, target it
explicitly or soft\-delete it first. Bulk mode also \fBnever touches a session
that is running in tmux\fP, soft\-deleted or not. With \fB\-\-deleted\fP,
targets only soft\-deleted sessions.
.RE
.TP
.BI "cs purge \-\-orphans" " [\-\-yes]"
Remove orphaned local state on this machine: \fB~/.claude/projects/\fP
directories whose decoded project path no longer exists on disk (the dirs
\fBcs sync\fP skips with a \fBcannot decode path\fP warning), plus DB records
on this host that point at a missing project path. This is the cleanup for the
cruft those skip\-warnings flag.
.RS
.PP
Without \fB\-\-yes\fP, lists what was found; removing more than one item also
requires a typed \fBYES\fP, same as \fBpurge \-\-all\fP.
.PP
Honors the same keep\-signal guard as bulk purge: a \fBlive \fB/rename\fPd or
tagged\fP session whose project path is gone (e.g. a transiently unmounted
drive) is listed but \fBkept\fP \(em target it explicitly with \fBcs purge
<name>\fP to remove it. Local\-only and irreversible.
.RE
.TP
.BI "cs add\-key" " [\-\-host <name>] [\-\-all]"
Load your SSH key into the shared cs agent and reset its lifetime, prompting
for the passphrase if needed. The agent is started only when its socket is
dead; a live agent is never killed.
.RS
.PP
Every cs session on a host shares one agent, so a single call covers all of
them \(em run it when the key timer has expired and SSH starts failing.
\fB\-\-host\fP runs it on a remote host; \fB\-\-all\fP on every known host.
.RE
.TP
.BI "cs agent stop" " [\-\-host <name>] [\-\-all]"
Kill the persistent SSH agent on one or all machines \(em useful when you are
done for the day and want keys out of memory. The agent runs at
\fB~/.ssh/cs\-agent.sock\fP and is started automatically by \fBcs attach\fP.
.RS
.PP
Because the agent is shared, stopping it cuts SSH access for every cs session
on that host at once.
.RE
.TP
.BI "cs update" " [\-\-force] [\-\-all]"
Check for a new version on the remote server and, if one is available,
download the updated bundle and man page. \fB\-\-force\fP re\-downloads even
when the version matches; \fB\-\-all\fP updates all known hosts via SSH after
updating locally. Also installs the periodic sync if it is not set up (unless
\fBnoCron\fP is set in config).
.RS
.PP
The downloaded bundle is verified against its published SHA\-256 checksum
before it replaces the running binary. A missing, malformed, or mismatched
checksum aborts the update and leaves the current binary untouched.
.PP
On its own, that checksum comes from the same origin as the bundle, so it
catches a corrupted download but not a compromised repo. Set \fBmirrorUrl\fP
in config (or \fBCS_MIRROR_URL\fP) to a second, independent host serving the
same files: the update then proceeds only if both origins publish the
identical checksum, and aborts if the mirror is unreachable, disagrees, or is
on the same host as the primary.
.RE
.TP
.BR "cs version" ", " "\-\-version"
Print the current version and exit.
.TP
.BR "cs \-\-help" ", " "\-h"
Display the usage summary and exit.
.\" END GENERATED COMMANDS
.SH SESSION TITLES
Sessions are automatically titled from the first human message in the
conversation. For example, if you started a session by typing "fix the nginx
config", that becomes the session title displayed in listings and the
dashboard. If a session name is set via
.B /rename
in Claude Code, that name takes priority and is also used as the tmux
session name.
.SH INSTALLATION
Install on any Linux host with:
.PP
.RS
.nf
curl -sSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kshartman/claude-session/main/install-remote.sh | bash
.fi
.RE
.PP
The installer verifies the downloaded bundle against its published SHA\-256
checksum before installing it, and registers a 5\-minute periodic sync (cron on
Linux, LaunchAgent on macOS). No shell profile is modified.
.PP
Options (pass via
.BR "bash -s --" ):
.TP
.B --nocron
Skip automatic cron sync setup.
.TP
.B --noconfig
Skip config copy from source host.
.PP
Override the repo URL with
.BR CS_REPO_URL :
.PP
.RS
.nf
CS_REPO_URL=https://your-host/path curl ... | bash
.fi
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is read from
.IR ~/.config/cs/config.json :
.PP
.RS
.nf
{
  "mongoUri": "mongodb://user:pass@host:27017/db?tls=true"
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
The file should be created with mode 0600 and the directory with mode 0700
to protect MongoDB credentials.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set, disables all ANSI color output. See
.IR https://no-color.org/ .
.TP
.B FORCE_COLOR
If set (and not
.BR 0 ),
enables color even when output is not a terminal, e.g.
.BR "cs list | less \-R" .
Without it, color is used only when standard output and standard error are
both terminals.
.B NO_COLOR
takes precedence.
.TP
.B CS_REPO_URL
Override the default repository URL for
.B cs update
and
.BR install-remote.sh .
Useful for self-hosted GitLab or GitHub instances.
.TP
.B CS_MIRROR_URL
A second, independent origin serving the same release files. When set,
.B cs update
and
.B install-remote.sh
require both origins to publish the identical bundle checksum, and abort if
the mirror is unreachable, disagrees, or is on the same host as the repo.
Overrides the
.I mirrorUrl
config setting.
.TP
.B CS_CONFIG_HOST
SSH hostname to copy config from during install (default:
.IR cs ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/cs/config.json
MongoDB connection configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.ssh/cs-agent.sock
Persistent SSH agent socket shared by every cs session on the host. Started
automatically by
.BR "cs attach" ;
keys expire after
.I agentKeyTimeout
seconds (default 8h). Reload with
.BR "cs add-key" ,
kill with
.BR "cs agent stop" .
.TP
.I ~/.claude/projects/<path-hash>/<session-id>.jsonl
Claude Code session files (read-only; cs never modifies these).
.TP
.I ~/.claude/projects/<path-hash>/<session-id>/session-memory/summary.md
Optional session summaries generated by Claude Code.
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/cs
The cs executable \(em a symlink to
.I cs.ts
for source installs, the downloaded bundle for remote installs.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (missing config, MongoDB failure, unknown command, ambiguous prefix,
missing dependency).
.SH EXAMPLES
Import existing sessions and view the dashboard:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cs sync
cs
.fi
.RE
.PP
Launch a persistent session and reconnect later:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cs launch myproject "refactor the auth module"
cs attach a3f7
.fi
.RE
.PP
See what's running across all hosts:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cs list
cs hosts
.fi
.RE
.PP
Attach to a session running on a different machine:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cs list
cs attach 952d    # auto-SSH if remote
.fi
.RE
.PP
Tag and search:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cs tag 952d auth-refactor
cs list --project myapp
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reload the SSH key after the 8h timer expires:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cs add-key
.fi
.RE
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.BR bun (1)
JavaScript/TypeScript runtime. Auto-installed by the remote installer if missing.
.TP
.BR tmux (1)
Terminal multiplexer. Required for launch, attach, kill, and status commands.
.TP
.BR fzf (1)
Fuzzy finder. Required only for the
.B resume
command.
.TP
.BR ssh (1)
Secure shell. Required only for remote attach.
.TP
.B MongoDB 5+
Central database for session metadata. TLS and SCRAM-SHA-256 authentication.
.SH BUGS
Session state detection is heuristic and may misclassify states when Claude
Code changes its terminal output format.
.PP
Path hash decoding uses recursive reconstruction to handle dots and hyphens
in directory names. Deeply nested paths with many ambiguous separators may
fail to decode; such sessions are skipped during sync with a warning.
.SH AUTHORS
Shane Hartman and Claude Code.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR claude (1),
.BR tmux (1),
.BR fzf (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR mongosh (1)
